{"team":"DAL","col":"#7FB0E8","identity":"balanced","funnel":"run-funnel","plays_pg":64.6,"adot":7.8,"report_html":"<div class=\"report\"><h2>Matchup-Driven</h2><p>They run downhill \u2014 mostly inside the tackles (20% to the edge vs ~25%), a gap/power scheme that trades big plays for a steady, grinding floor.</p><h3>The Offensive Blueprint</h3><p>They play fast \u2014 <strong>65 snaps a game</strong> (league ~61), and the extra volume is a rising tide that lifts everyone's counting stats.</p><h3>In the Red Zone</h3><p>Inside the 20 they stay aggressive, throwing <strong>58%</strong> of the time, which puts scoring equity on <strong>George Pickens</strong>.</p><h2>Defense \u2014 The Run Comes Free</h2><p><strong>Soft against backs out of the backfield</strong> \u2014 29 rec yds/game (vs ~18). A rec-yards target.</p><p>They surrender <strong>133 rushing</strong> and <strong>252 passing</strong> yards per game (league ~120 / ~230). The run moves against them \u2014 <strong>target opposing RB1s</strong>.</p><p><strong>Soft against opposing WR2s</strong> \u2014 43 rec yds/game (vs ~36). A rec-yards target.</p><p>They leak <strong>WR1 receiving TDs</strong> (0.59/game vs ~0.38) \u2014 an anytime-TD spot to attack.</p><p>They leak <strong>RB rushing TDs</strong> (0.62/game vs ~0.46) \u2014 an anytime-TD spot to attack.</p><p>Broadly a leaky unit \u2014 47% success rate allowed (vs ~44%); points come easy against them.</p><h2>The Betting Angles</h2><p>Bottom line: <strong>opposing RB1s</strong> smash on the ground and at the goal line.</p><p><em>Built on 2024\u201325 data; the profile rebuilds through the season as the current staff and roster set their own tendencies.</em></p></div>","depth":{"QB":[{"name":"Dak Prescott","slot":"QB1","starter":true,"td":9,"props":{"Comp":21.4,"Att":31.56,"Pass Yds":234.9,"Pass TD":1.8,"INT":0.61,"Rush Yds":11.76},"d":{"completions":21.4,"attempts":31.56,"pass_yards":234.9,"pass_td":1.8,"interceptions":0.61,"rush_att":2.95,"rush_yards":11